1
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:22,147
This is your chance to escape from here.

2
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:26,875
But if you do that,
you must not show yourself to them.

3
00:00:26,875 --> 00:00:29,912
For sure,
your grandfather and your daddy will look for you.

4
00:00:29,912 --> 00:00:32,748
Why do you have a drawing of Mr. Samuel?

5
00:00:32,748 --> 00:00:33,982
- Samuel?
- Samuel?

6
00:00:33,982 --> 00:00:35,617
Yes, he often comes here.

7
00:00:35,617 --> 00:00:38,353
That's Mr. Samuel. Samuel Almero.

8
00:00:38,353 --> 00:00:41,183
You know, Lorenzo, it's all your fault.

9
00:00:41,183 --> 00:00:42,824
You're the reason why Florence is rebelling.

10
00:00:42,824 --> 00:00:45,093
Don't interfere with family matters.

11
00:00:45,093 --> 00:00:47,151
Your anger won't help right now.

12
00:00:47,151 --> 00:00:52,200
What's important is
we have to figure out where Florence went.

13
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,869
I think I have an idea where she went.

14
00:00:53,869 --> 00:00:56,805
I do hope Florence is here.

15
00:00:56,805 --> 00:01:00,075
I hope she went back to our house.

16
00:01:00,075 --> 00:01:03,979
Because if that happens,
I will never give her back to you.

17
00:01:03,979 --> 00:01:06,081
Even if you kill me.

18
00:01:06,081 --> 00:01:07,849
You can never get my daughter back.

19
00:01:07,849 --> 00:01:09,851
The reason why I brought them here,

20
00:01:09,851 --> 00:01:11,753
is because I told them
to talk about their plan.

21
00:01:11,753 --> 00:01:13,221
- Plan?
- What plan?

22
00:01:13,221 --> 00:01:18,460
We plan to go to a faraway place.
To elope and live together.

23
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:20,422
Away from all these problems.

24
00:01:20,422 --> 00:01:22,526
What?

25
00:02:09,711 --> 00:02:14,983
Maybe Alyanna escaped from you that night.

26
00:02:14,983 --> 00:02:17,352
She knew the situation was dangerous,
that's why she couldn't do anything,

27
00:02:17,352 --> 00:02:19,504
but protect her daughter!

28
00:02:20,989 --> 00:02:22,557
Well, I didn't eat.

29
00:02:22,557 --> 00:02:23,959
What do you mean you didn't eat?

30
00:02:23,959 --> 00:02:27,161
I ordered three cups of rice,
but you took another one.

31
00:02:27,161 --> 00:02:29,177
If you think about it.

32
00:02:29,177 --> 00:02:31,767
Wait, I feel dizzy.

33
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:34,703
Oh no, that's what I'm telling you.

34
00:02:34,703 --> 00:02:37,773
Okay, let's drink medicine later.

35
00:02:37,773 --> 00:02:39,207
What medicine?

36
00:02:39,207 --> 00:02:41,926
Well, I'll take care of it.

37
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:49,640
Mister, have you seen a woman pass by here?

38
00:02:51,019 --> 00:02:52,537
No.

39
00:02:53,455 --> 00:02:54,489
No?

40
00:02:54,489 --> 00:02:56,132
No.

41
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,452
Okay, thank you.

42
00:03:03,031 --> 00:03:05,036
What's his problem?

43
00:03:09,337 --> 00:03:11,022
- Did you hear that?
- Was that you?

44
00:03:11,809 --> 00:03:13,608
That's not me.

45
00:03:13,608 --> 00:03:14,992
- What was that?
- What was that?

46
00:03:18,126 --> 00:03:20,344
Oh no. Is that a cricket?

47
00:03:24,639 --> 00:03:27,222
- Something is moving at the back.
- Huh?

48
00:03:27,222 --> 00:03:28,606
What's that?

49
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:53,817
Enough with this madness!

50
00:03:54,716 --> 00:03:59,187
This is clearly a blatant attempt
to tear my family apart.

51
00:03:59,187 --> 00:04:00,638
Let's leave.

52
00:04:01,934 --> 00:04:02,991
Lorenzo!

53
00:04:02,991 --> 00:04:04,209
- Hey, wait.
- It's okay.

54
00:04:04,209 --> 00:04:06,555
It's okay. Lorenzo...

55
00:04:06,555 --> 00:04:10,753
If you love Alyanna,
you will find out the truth.

56
00:04:10,753 --> 00:04:14,039
Because only the truth can protect Florence.

57
00:04:26,781 --> 00:04:28,817
They really have the nerve.

58
00:04:28,817 --> 00:04:30,886
I'm the one who's being reasonable.

59
00:04:30,886 --> 00:04:33,538
I'm the one who's being accused of something.

60
00:04:35,524 --> 00:04:37,139
- Lorenzo!
- Is it true?

61
00:04:37,139 --> 00:04:39,591
Were you there when Alyanna was killed?

62
00:04:40,695 --> 00:04:42,497
Lorenzo, come on. Do you believe them more?

63
00:04:42,497 --> 00:04:44,259
Answer me!

64
00:04:44,259 --> 00:04:46,608
Is it true? Why can't you answer?

65
00:04:46,608 --> 00:04:49,137
It's a simple yes or no question.

66
00:04:49,137 --> 00:04:51,973
Were you there when my wife was killed?

67
00:04:51,973 --> 00:04:55,032
Do you believe them more than me, Lorenzo?

68
00:04:55,032 --> 00:04:56,378
Do you see me as your brother?

69
00:04:56,378 --> 00:04:58,062
That's enough!

70
00:04:59,069 --> 00:05:01,550
Let's go home first.

71
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:04,735
Let's find out the root of all of this.

72
00:05:09,634 --> 00:05:12,394
If Federico is telling the truth...

73
00:05:12,394 --> 00:05:15,480
you have a lot of explaining to do, Samuel!

74
00:05:18,967 --> 00:05:21,403
Dad? Dad?

75
00:05:21,403 --> 00:05:23,905
Baste! Baste, start the car.

76
00:05:23,905 --> 00:05:25,389
Come on, get inside the car.

77
00:05:32,814 --> 00:05:37,101
Really?
You will really tolerate their plan to elope?

78
00:05:37,786 --> 00:05:38,961
I mean, why not?

79
00:05:38,961 --> 00:05:42,875
God gave us free will,
and what better way to use our free will,

80
00:05:42,875 --> 00:05:46,027
than to spend the rest of our lives
with the person we love.

81
00:05:46,027 --> 00:05:47,095
- That's right.
- That's right.

82
00:05:47,095 --> 00:05:48,129
Right?

83
00:05:48,129 --> 00:05:50,031
Cheers, guys.

84
00:05:50,031 --> 00:05:52,636
I can't believe that Nero is capable,

85
00:05:52,636 --> 00:05:58,440
unlike other guys that I know
who are quiet when it comes to romance.

86
00:05:58,440 --> 00:06:00,291
Are you challenging me?

87
00:06:02,347 --> 00:06:04,913
Nero, I'm so happy for you.

88
00:06:04,913 --> 00:06:10,334
That is why I now know
why Antonia was so obsessed with you.

89
00:06:10,991 --> 00:06:12,754
Ouch, Camille.

90
00:06:12,754 --> 00:06:17,425
I wonder when I can graduate
from your "crazy ex-girlfriend" punchline.

91
00:06:17,425 --> 00:06:23,398
- Well...
- No, but I really do agree. I'm impressed.

92
00:06:23,398 --> 00:06:25,742
And if ever things don't work out...

93
00:06:25,742 --> 00:06:28,628
I can definitely be next in line, Nero.

94
00:06:30,715 --> 00:06:32,311
That's okay, bro.

95
00:06:33,182 --> 00:06:35,217
- Just joking.
- My gosh.

96
00:06:36,711 --> 00:06:40,782
Who said romance is dead?

97
00:06:40,782 --> 00:06:42,083
Why?

98
00:06:42,083 --> 00:06:44,419
Do you want us to elope too?

99
00:06:44,419 --> 00:06:46,254
- Of course not.
- Oh my gosh!

100
00:06:46,254 --> 00:06:48,734
Exactly the point.

101
00:06:48,734 --> 00:06:51,993
Eloping is the most stupid thing to do.

102
00:06:51,993 --> 00:06:53,789
Why do they have to elope?

103
00:06:53,789 --> 00:06:57,719
Just face the problem
and find ways to keep loving each other.

104
00:06:57,719 --> 00:07:01,372
Running away is the most selfish thing
one can do.

105
00:07:02,724 --> 00:07:05,393
That's what you get from watching K-dramas.

106
00:07:05,393 --> 00:07:07,896
It's all romance and thrill.

107
00:07:07,896 --> 00:07:09,764
You're not thinking.

108
00:07:09,764 --> 00:07:12,701
- You're such a killjoy, Bro.
- Bitter.

109
00:07:12,701 --> 00:07:14,736
Boo, Tristan.

110
00:07:14,736 --> 00:07:17,372
Maybe you should take a page
from Nero's playbook.

111
00:07:17,372 --> 00:07:20,658
And learn
that sometimes, life can be about love.

112
00:07:21,343 --> 00:07:24,662
You know, you should stop picking on Tristan.

113
00:07:26,514 --> 00:07:28,633
I was being impulsive.

114
00:07:29,284 --> 00:07:31,820
I hated the idea that everything I want,

115
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:35,664
all my decisions,
are controlled by my new family.

116
00:07:35,664 --> 00:07:38,470
What I should be feeling right now
is I should be thrilled

117
00:07:38,470 --> 00:07:41,445
because I just entered
into my first relationship.

118
00:07:42,063 --> 00:07:44,399
Your first and last relationship.

119
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:46,468
Oh my gosh.

120
00:07:46,468 --> 00:07:47,652
There!

121
00:07:48,703 --> 00:07:51,188
But Tristan is right, Nero.

122
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:54,909
I got carried away by my emotions.

123
00:07:54,909 --> 00:07:58,763
I couldn't get what I want,
that's why I escaped and ran away.

124
00:07:59,447 --> 00:08:02,967
If you didn't see me,
maybe I'd be in Baguio by now.

125
00:08:03,785 --> 00:08:05,820
But now that I get to spend time
with all of you,

126
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,838
even for a short time...

127
00:08:08,556 --> 00:08:10,675
I was able to think.

128
00:08:12,794 --> 00:08:14,679
You're right, Tristan.

129
00:08:17,386 --> 00:08:20,005
Running away is very selfish.

130
00:08:23,972 --> 00:08:29,126
And you can't easily escape
all these complications.

131
00:08:30,174 --> 00:08:32,959
It's difficult, but I have to.

132
00:08:34,015 --> 00:08:37,385
And it seems that's what I need to do.

133
00:08:37,385 --> 00:08:39,737
To face all my problems.

134
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:43,591
So...

135
00:08:43,591 --> 00:08:45,176
Nero?

136
00:08:45,827 --> 00:08:51,499
I'm sorry, but it seems
we're not pushing through.

137
00:08:51,499 --> 00:08:56,271
Let's cancel our plans
of living in a nipa hut...

138
00:08:56,271 --> 00:09:01,125
by the beach with our pet dog and cat.

139
00:09:06,848 --> 00:09:10,134
You know I will support you
in all of your decisions.

140
00:09:12,587 --> 00:09:14,438
You know what this means, right?

141
00:09:15,056 --> 00:09:18,993
If you go back to your dad,
he'll probably take you to the States.

142
00:09:18,993 --> 00:09:22,230
Guys, this is probably the last time

143
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:25,116
we'll be able to spend time with Florence.

144
00:09:29,237 --> 00:09:30,939
Last?

145
00:09:30,939 --> 00:09:32,957
As in final, final?

146
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:37,028
Yes.

147
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:43,200
No way.

148
00:10:14,015 --> 00:10:16,400
Dad, take this.

149
00:10:34,469 --> 00:10:36,854
I'm sorry for what happened earlier.

150
00:10:37,806 --> 00:10:40,024
I just couldn't control myself.

151
00:10:44,641 --> 00:10:46,359
Tell me, Lorenzo...

152
00:10:48,149 --> 00:10:53,604
Do you honestly believe Samuel
has something to do with Alyanna's death?

153
00:10:57,992 --> 00:10:59,719
You know...

154
00:11:02,324 --> 00:11:04,086
I don't know what to think.

155
00:11:05,867 --> 00:11:09,620
It seems Federico's accusation is absurd.

156
00:11:13,208 --> 00:11:15,793
I can't explain it, Dad, but...

157
00:11:18,049 --> 00:11:19,967
the accusation?

158
00:11:23,330 --> 00:11:25,649
It all made sense to me.

159
00:11:26,502 --> 00:11:29,014
Samuel is your brother!

160
00:11:32,747 --> 00:11:36,287
You're suspecting a family member.

161
00:11:38,469 --> 00:11:39,861
I know.

162
00:11:41,166 --> 00:11:44,005
That's why I wanted him to deny it.

163
00:11:44,005 --> 00:11:46,207
I wanted him to tell me to my face,

164
00:11:46,207 --> 00:11:49,210
that all the accusations against him
were not true.

165
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:52,396
For whatever reason, Dad...

166
00:11:53,481 --> 00:11:55,913
I have a strong feeling,

167
00:11:55,913 --> 00:12:00,538
Samuel has something to do with
what happened to my wife and daughter.

168
00:12:05,426 --> 00:12:07,311
Talk to Baste.

169
00:12:07,983 --> 00:12:10,274
Do it discreetly.

170
00:12:11,766 --> 00:12:17,064
I don't want anyone to hear
or know what we're about to do.

171
00:12:20,174 --> 00:12:23,556
I want Samuel investigated.

172
00:12:24,317 --> 00:12:27,169
I want to know everything about him.

173
00:12:29,319 --> 00:12:33,072
Dig up everything that he is hiding.

174
00:12:34,956 --> 00:12:37,841
And I want you to talk to Federico as well.

175
00:12:39,027 --> 00:12:42,964
Find out all the details
you can get from him.

176
00:12:42,964 --> 00:12:46,134
And then I want you to talk to our people.

177
00:12:46,134 --> 00:12:49,003
And I want you to have them
interview everybody,

178
00:12:49,003 --> 00:12:52,556
all the people in that area.

179
00:12:54,244 --> 00:12:59,465
If it's true
that someone saw or recognized Samuel...

180
00:13:02,916 --> 00:13:03,634
If it's proven

181
00:13:03,634 --> 00:13:07,203
that Samuel has something
to do with Alyanna's death...

182
00:13:11,352 --> 00:13:14,038
I'm going to make sure that he pays for it.

183
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:40,723
Are you sure
it was Samuel who you remembered?

184
00:13:41,419 --> 00:13:48,029
He sure is, Don Ferell,
because Federico hadn't met Samuel...

185
00:13:48,029 --> 00:13:53,117
but he was able to describe
and draw the face of that animal.

186
00:13:54,562 --> 00:13:56,854
You were able to draw him? Let me see.

187
00:14:04,946 --> 00:14:06,523
Where?

188
00:14:09,867 --> 00:14:11,251
What?

189
00:14:12,092 --> 00:14:14,881
How can this be Samuel?

190
00:14:14,881 --> 00:14:18,309
Babycakes, turn the page.

191
00:14:26,801 --> 00:14:29,404
I wasn't the only one who recognized him.

192
00:14:29,404 --> 00:14:32,027
A lot of people saw and recognized him

193
00:14:32,027 --> 00:14:34,458
in the area where Alyanna was killed.

194
00:14:37,912 --> 00:14:41,015
Why did he flaunt his face there?

195
00:14:41,015 --> 00:14:45,153
If just in case I'd committed a crime,
I won't go back there.

196
00:14:45,153 --> 00:14:47,088
And why would you commit a crime?

197
00:14:47,088 --> 00:14:48,956
I said just in case.

198
00:14:48,956 --> 00:14:51,225
I think he was looking for the baby.

199
00:14:51,225 --> 00:14:53,561
He was looking for Florence.

200
00:14:53,561 --> 00:14:58,420
It just so happened
that Alyanna was able to hide the baby.

201
00:14:59,667 --> 00:15:01,920
That's what we thought too.

202
00:15:04,233 --> 00:15:08,691
I think he's using the kid for the ransom.

203
00:15:08,691 --> 00:15:12,714
Imagine that. He is fooling his own father.

204
00:15:12,714 --> 00:15:15,542
We cannot go by assumptions.

205
00:15:15,542 --> 00:15:19,687
Serafica, call our people.
I want a legal team assembled.

206
00:15:19,687 --> 00:15:22,356
And also get a good investigator.

207
00:15:22,356 --> 00:15:26,894
That Samuel Almero
should be investigated properly.

208
00:15:26,894 --> 00:15:32,010
I want to have correct evidence
that we can show to Don Almero

209
00:15:32,010 --> 00:15:34,102
the next time I see him.

210
00:15:34,102 --> 00:15:37,121
Yes, Sir. I'll do that first thing tomorrow.

211
00:15:37,872 --> 00:15:40,438
I'll get to the bottom of this.

212
00:15:40,438 --> 00:15:43,377
I'll make sure that Florence is safe.

213
00:15:43,377 --> 00:15:48,366
It's a blessing
that Florence ran away from them.

214
00:15:48,366 --> 00:15:50,702
That's right.

215
00:15:50,702 --> 00:15:53,221
At least now, she is far from Samuel.

216
00:15:53,221 --> 00:15:54,605
She is safe.

217
00:15:55,223 --> 00:15:57,631
Maybe she's not only safe...

218
00:15:57,631 --> 00:16:00,128
but safer?

219
00:16:00,128 --> 00:16:03,053
Safest, safer-est.

220
00:16:05,333 --> 00:16:07,802
- That's what I'm saying.
- That's it.

221
00:16:07,802 --> 00:16:09,170
You keep saying it over and over.

222
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:10,471
Yes.

223
00:16:10,471 --> 00:16:13,040
And where have you all been?

224
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:15,910
A lot of things are happening here

225
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:18,045
and you managed to go out and have fun.

226
00:16:18,045 --> 00:16:19,680
Relax.

227
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:22,984
We didn't go out and have fun, Ms. Serafica.

228
00:16:22,984 --> 00:16:25,853
Actually, we met up with Florence.

229
00:16:25,853 --> 00:16:27,304
Florence?

230
00:16:28,055 --> 00:16:29,390
Where is she?

231
00:16:29,390 --> 00:16:30,892
Don't worry, Auntie. She's okay.

232
00:16:30,892 --> 00:16:32,193
Relax.

233
00:16:32,193 --> 00:16:34,962
She was planning to run away,
but we were able to convince her.

234
00:16:34,962 --> 00:16:37,446
She's on her way back to the Almeros.

235
00:16:38,666 --> 00:16:40,517
What?

236
00:16:44,275 --> 00:16:46,110
Did I say something?

237
00:16:52,246 --> 00:16:56,080
I'm hopeful that they will listen to me.

238
00:16:56,080 --> 00:17:00,288
I will try to convince them
not to send me to the States.

239
00:17:00,288 --> 00:17:02,583
What if they won't agree?

240
00:17:03,524 --> 00:17:05,393
Well, then...

241
00:17:05,393 --> 00:17:08,229
I will follow your advice.

242
00:17:08,229 --> 00:17:12,867
Sometimes love is enduring, so...

243
00:17:12,867 --> 00:17:15,169
I'll just have to endure.

244
00:17:15,169 --> 00:17:18,139
I may be far from you, but...

245
00:17:18,139 --> 00:17:20,657
my love won't stop.

246
00:17:24,078 --> 00:17:26,021
Don't worry, Florence.

247
00:17:26,021 --> 00:17:29,483
I'll convince Grandpa Garp
to let me transfer to the States.

248
00:17:29,483 --> 00:17:31,252
Are you sure?

249
00:17:31,252 --> 00:17:33,821
There are a lot of English speakers there.

250
00:17:33,821 --> 00:17:36,457
I will always be true to my promise.

251
00:17:36,457 --> 00:17:38,609
To be always by your side.

252
00:17:39,758 --> 00:17:41,762
Wow.

253
00:17:41,762 --> 00:17:44,973
Please, take it easy with your sweetness.

254
00:17:44,973 --> 00:17:47,362
I'm already diabetic, won't you pity me?

255
00:17:47,362 --> 00:17:49,753
I've been with you both for a long time.

256
00:17:53,581 --> 00:17:55,464
Grandpa is calling.

257
00:17:55,464 --> 00:17:56,911
Hello?

258
00:17:56,911 --> 00:17:58,679
Nero, listen.

259
00:17:58,679 --> 00:18:02,383
Don't ever let Florence
go back to the Almeros.

260
00:18:02,383 --> 00:18:04,089
Grandpa? Hello?

261
00:18:05,319 --> 00:18:07,822
Her life is in danger.

262
00:18:07,822 --> 00:18:11,025
Her uncle, Samuel, he's the killer.

263
00:18:11,025 --> 00:18:13,127
What did Grandpa say? Is he looking for us?

264
00:18:13,127 --> 00:18:14,929
My phone suddenly died.

265
00:18:14,929 --> 00:18:16,931
Maybe he's worried.

266
00:18:16,931 --> 00:18:19,233
Maybe he's been calling me.

267
00:18:19,233 --> 00:18:21,469
Wait, I'll just get my phone in the car.

268
00:18:21,469 --> 00:18:24,805
Wait, let's take Florence home first.

269
00:18:24,805 --> 00:18:26,607
Okay.

270
00:18:26,607 --> 00:18:31,245
Well, just tell them what happened,

271
00:18:31,245 --> 00:18:32,813
so they will always be updated

272
00:18:32,813 --> 00:18:35,933
on the latest showbiz events and happenings.

273
00:18:40,721 --> 00:18:42,675
Uncle Samuel?

274
00:18:44,759 --> 00:18:46,741
Uncle Samuel!

275
00:18:50,202 --> 00:18:51,989
Florence.

276
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:57,378
What happened to you?

277
00:18:58,039 --> 00:18:59,740
This? Well, this is nothing.

278
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:02,677
How about you? Why are you still here?
I already helped you escape.

279
00:19:02,677 --> 00:19:04,378
Why did you come back?

280
00:19:04,378 --> 00:19:06,247
Didn't you miss me?

281
00:19:06,247 --> 00:19:08,122
Don't you want me here?

282
00:19:08,122 --> 00:19:10,724
Don't you want my scrambled eggs anymore,

283
00:19:10,724 --> 00:19:14,088
and the food I cook for you?

284
00:19:14,088 --> 00:19:16,891
Nero, Tristan, he is Uncle Samuel.

285
00:19:16,891 --> 00:19:19,694
My favorite uncle.

286
00:19:19,694 --> 00:19:22,596
Well, he is my only uncle,

287
00:19:22,596 --> 00:19:26,316
but that won't diminish
the favor I hold for him.

288
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:31,254
Is there a problem?

289
00:19:34,592 --> 00:19:37,051
Nothing...

290
00:19:37,051 --> 00:19:38,913
It's...

291
00:19:38,913 --> 00:19:41,882
your Grandpa Roger.

292
00:19:41,882 --> 00:19:44,685
He had a heart attack.

293
00:19:44,685 --> 00:19:46,821
He's in the hospital right now.

294
00:19:46,821 --> 00:19:48,363
That's why...

295
00:19:49,223 --> 00:19:50,691
you need to go with me.

296
00:19:50,691 --> 00:19:52,442
Come on, let's go to him.

297
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:55,196
We'll go with you.

298
00:19:55,196 --> 00:19:57,097
- Okay.
- Let's go. Hurry.

299
00:20:21,188 --> 00:20:23,357
Still nothing?

300
00:20:23,357 --> 00:20:26,805
Tristan is still not answering.

301
00:20:28,896 --> 00:20:31,532
Dencio, Iking, let's go to them.

302
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:32,466
- Try again.
- Come on. Let's go!

303
00:20:32,466 --> 00:20:33,567
- Take care.
- Just stay here.

304
00:20:33,567 --> 00:20:35,756
You are more needed here.

305
00:20:51,452 --> 00:20:53,721
Uncle Samuel, what happened to Grandpa?

306
00:20:53,721 --> 00:20:55,189
Why did he suffer a heart attack?

307
00:20:55,189 --> 00:20:57,391
Is it because I ran away?

308
00:20:57,391 --> 00:20:58,959
This is my fault.

309
00:20:58,959 --> 00:21:00,461
Florence, Florence.

310
00:21:00,461 --> 00:21:02,196
It's not your fault.

311
00:21:02,196 --> 00:21:04,398
And I'm sure he'll be okay.

312
00:21:04,398 --> 00:21:06,183
What if he's not?

313
00:21:07,368 --> 00:21:11,439
I can't forgive myself
if something bad happens to him.

314
00:21:11,439 --> 00:21:12,956
Florence...

315
00:21:13,774 --> 00:21:15,676
Nero is right.

316
00:21:15,676 --> 00:21:17,260
Don't worry.

317
00:21:19,146 --> 00:21:22,632
Wait, why weren't you with them
in the hospital?

318
00:21:26,387 --> 00:21:27,704
Nothing...

319
00:21:28,541 --> 00:21:30,558
I needed to go home.

320
00:21:30,558 --> 00:21:32,542
I needed to get some things.

321
00:21:43,504 --> 00:21:44,738
Wait.

322
00:21:44,738 --> 00:21:47,390
Where is this hospital you're saying?

323
00:21:50,144 --> 00:21:52,763
Just over there.
It's the Mary Grace Hospital.

324
00:21:58,385 --> 00:22:02,139
Wait, we're not going there.
This is going out of Levante.

325
00:22:11,932 --> 00:22:13,116
Get off the car.

326
00:22:14,401 --> 00:22:16,303
Uncle Samuel, why do you have that?

327
00:22:16,303 --> 00:22:18,439
Don't ask too many questions.
Get off the car!

328
00:22:18,439 --> 00:22:19,306
Get down!

329
00:22:19,306 --> 00:22:20,307
- What?
- Don't move!

330
00:22:20,307 --> 00:22:22,209
Do you want to fight back?

331
00:22:22,209 --> 00:22:24,845
I said get off the car. Get off the car!

332
00:22:24,845 --> 00:22:26,463
I said get off.

333
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:34,277
Stay here.

334
00:22:37,424 --> 00:22:39,183
I said, here.

335
00:22:42,496 --> 00:22:44,565
Uncle Samuel, what's this?

336
00:22:44,565 --> 00:22:46,898
Why are you doing this?

337
00:22:48,328 --> 00:22:50,210
It's clear.

338
00:22:50,210 --> 00:22:52,306
He's planning something bad.

339
00:22:52,306 --> 00:22:54,632
Shut up, kid.

340
00:22:59,847 --> 00:23:02,068
Where is Grandpa Roger?

341
00:23:03,350 --> 00:23:05,686
Don't worry about your grandpa.

342
00:23:05,686 --> 00:23:07,350
He's safe.

343
00:23:08,689 --> 00:23:10,436
But you know what?

344
00:23:11,125 --> 00:23:13,410
All of this wouldn't have happened...

345
00:23:14,094 --> 00:23:17,798
if not for your father figure, Federico.

346
00:23:17,798 --> 00:23:20,000
I don't understand.

347
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,169
What does Father have to do with this?

348
00:23:22,169 --> 00:23:26,907
He remembered and saw what happened...
the night Alyanna died.

349
00:23:26,907 --> 00:23:31,127
And he's saying that I killed your mother.

350
00:23:34,114 --> 00:23:37,218
But I think there's nothing I can do.

351
00:23:37,218 --> 00:23:41,938
I can't get away with
the secrets that I've kept.

352
00:23:44,125 --> 00:23:47,310
Because your grandfather and daddy...

353
00:23:47,962 --> 00:23:50,731
are having me investigated.

354
00:23:50,731 --> 00:23:52,282
I'm sure...

355
00:23:53,867 --> 00:23:59,189
your Grandpa Garpidio
will dig up all my secrets.

356
00:24:01,609 --> 00:24:04,678
Tomorrow or the day after...

357
00:24:04,678 --> 00:24:07,464
they'll find out about my secret.

358
00:24:14,588 --> 00:24:15,994
Mister, what's happening?

359
00:24:15,994 --> 00:24:17,830
I don't know.

360
00:24:20,908 --> 00:24:22,752
What are you doing?

361
00:25:02,336 --> 00:25:04,287
I'm sorry, Celestina.

362
00:25:05,557 --> 00:25:07,942
Mommy has to go.

363
00:25:09,310 --> 00:25:11,583
Just stay here first.

364
00:25:15,881 --> 00:25:19,263
I love you so much. I love you, Celestina.

365
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:34,902
Let's go, you're sleepy.

366
00:25:34,902 --> 00:25:37,071
Your head hurts, let's go home.

367
00:25:37,071 --> 00:25:38,855
- Let's go.
- I feel dizzy.

368
00:25:45,045 --> 00:25:46,613
Mister?

369
00:25:46,613 --> 00:25:49,232
Have you seen a woman pass by here?

370
00:25:50,584 --> 00:25:51,901
No.

371
00:25:52,853 --> 00:25:54,007
No?

372
00:25:54,007 --> 00:25:55,538
No.

373
00:25:58,225 --> 00:26:00,053
Okay, thank you.

374
00:26:02,061 --> 00:26:05,749
What? He suddenly appeared.

375
00:26:18,545 --> 00:26:19,847
Samuel!

376
00:26:19,847 --> 00:26:21,398
Samuel, please.

377
00:26:22,149 --> 00:26:24,567
Don't do this.

378
00:26:28,288 --> 00:26:31,074
Why are you inside the car?

379
00:26:34,395 --> 00:26:36,584
And not Lorenzo?

380
00:26:39,500 --> 00:26:41,022
Alyanna...

381
00:26:43,303 --> 00:26:45,388
I have to do this.

382
00:26:48,409 --> 00:26:51,738
Because you'll tell them everything I did.

383
00:26:58,252 --> 00:27:02,839
What did Lorenzo do to you?
Why do you have to hurt him?

384
00:27:03,757 --> 00:27:05,993
Samuel, Lorenzo is your brother.

385
00:27:05,993 --> 00:27:09,333
We're one family.

386
00:27:11,965 --> 00:27:13,450
Family?

387
00:27:15,769 --> 00:27:17,814
Are you really a part of my family?

388
00:27:18,639 --> 00:27:20,924
Are you really all my family?

389
00:27:23,977 --> 00:27:26,980
As long as Lorenzo's alive...

390
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:29,966
I will never get what I deserve.

391
00:27:32,415 --> 00:27:34,259
Whatever I do...

392
00:27:35,674 --> 00:27:37,825
Daddy only loves him.

393
00:27:40,595 --> 00:27:42,846
Whatever sacrifices I do...

394
00:27:43,897 --> 00:27:47,093
I know he will still get everything.

395
00:27:52,873 --> 00:27:55,892
Don't do this, Samuel.

396
00:27:58,111 --> 00:28:01,939
I'm begging you.

397
00:28:05,085 --> 00:28:08,138
You're not a bad person.

398
00:28:09,289 --> 00:28:12,993
Don't let that anger in your heart
eat you up.

399
00:28:12,993 --> 00:28:15,545
Please, don't.

400
00:28:21,401 --> 00:28:23,881
I'm sorry, Alyanna...

401
00:28:28,015 --> 00:28:30,444
But don't worry.

402
00:28:30,444 --> 00:28:33,178
I will look for Celestina.

403
00:28:34,809 --> 00:28:37,928
- No...
- I will always protect her.

404
00:29:00,507 --> 00:29:08,880
That I was the one who killed your mother.

405
00:29:12,986 --> 00:29:16,639
That's why when I saw you having a hard time
under Lorenzo's care.

406
00:29:18,156 --> 00:29:21,461
Florence, I helped you so you can escape.

407
00:29:21,461 --> 00:29:23,346
So, you can be free, right?

408
00:29:24,498 --> 00:29:25,971
Right?

409
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:29,552
Because that's what I promised Alyanna.

410
00:29:31,277 --> 00:29:33,257
So that somehow...

411
00:29:34,408 --> 00:29:36,693
I can pay...

412
00:29:39,012 --> 00:29:40,797
for what I did to her.

413
00:29:48,989 --> 00:29:52,402
Is this your way of protecting me?

414
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:55,399
Florence...

415
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,864
I will not hurt you.

416
00:29:57,864 --> 00:29:59,315
Don't worry.

417
00:30:00,713 --> 00:30:04,199
But don't you dare
do something I wouldn't like.

418
00:30:05,439 --> 00:30:07,023
Because if not...

419
00:30:07,975 --> 00:30:12,062
I might not be able
to fulfill what I promised your mother.

420
00:30:14,982 --> 00:30:19,019
Florence, I just need you, so I can escape.

421
00:30:19,019 --> 00:30:22,205
So I can get money
from your grandfather and your dad.

422
00:30:22,889 --> 00:30:25,959
Because I want to start anew...

423
00:30:25,959 --> 00:30:27,910
and live far away from all of you.

424
00:30:30,697 --> 00:30:33,716
Good thing you brought a Ferell with you.

425
00:30:35,002 --> 00:30:38,171
I'll earn more with this.

426
00:30:38,171 --> 00:30:39,856
You will not win.

427
00:30:40,474 --> 00:30:42,225
Wherever you go...

428
00:30:42,843 --> 00:30:44,878
you'll pay for all your sins.

429
00:30:44,878 --> 00:30:46,089
Why?

430
00:30:46,847 --> 00:30:49,583
What do you know about my sins?

431
00:30:49,583 --> 00:30:51,556
What do you know?

432
00:30:53,520 --> 00:30:55,772
You're so young.

433
00:30:58,625 --> 00:31:01,044
Do you want me to make you an example?

434
00:31:02,663 --> 00:31:06,215
If all my plans don't push through...

435
00:31:08,502 --> 00:31:14,457
the Ferells and Almeros will pay me
a huge amount of money.

436
00:31:15,509 --> 00:31:16,877
Move over, Florence.

437
00:31:16,877 --> 00:31:21,481
- No, Uncle Samuel. Don't.
- Move over, Florence. Move.

438
00:31:21,481 --> 00:31:23,733
- Tristan!
- Tristan, don't!

439
00:31:25,485 --> 00:31:26,920
- Tristan, don't!
- Uncle Samuel, stop it!

440
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:28,705
Enough, please.

441
00:31:29,623 --> 00:31:31,874
- Tristan!
- Tristan, don't!

442
00:31:32,659 --> 00:31:34,339
Tristan!

443
00:31:43,170 --> 00:31:46,089
- Tristan!
- Tristan!

444
00:31:51,211 --> 00:31:52,782
Tristan...

445
00:31:54,514 --> 00:31:56,132
Don't worry.

446
00:31:57,250 --> 00:31:58,801
You're safe now.

447
00:32:00,420 --> 00:32:01,834
Tristan?

448
00:32:14,868 --> 00:32:16,352
Tristan?

449
00:32:17,104 --> 00:32:18,287
Hey...

450
00:32:22,442 --> 00:32:25,612
- Tristan? Hey!
- Help!

451
00:32:25,612 --> 00:32:28,448
- Help us!
- Help!

452
00:32:28,448 --> 00:32:31,852
- Tristan, hey!
- Tristan, wake up!

453
00:32:31,852 --> 00:32:33,896
Help!

454
00:32:33,896 --> 00:32:35,555
Help us!

455
00:32:35,555 --> 00:32:37,183
Help!

456
00:32:37,183 --> 00:32:39,192
Help us!

457
00:32:39,192 --> 00:32:42,678
- Hey, wake up!
- Help!

458
00:32:43,396 --> 00:32:46,149
- Help!
- Help!

459
00:33:00,545 --> 00:33:02,233
Florence...

460
00:33:02,234 --> 00:33:03,861
is this okay?

461
00:33:03,861 --> 00:33:05,916
- Just one more, Mother.
- Okay.

462
00:33:07,118 --> 00:33:08,501
Where is Dencio?

463
00:33:08,501 --> 00:33:12,967
- Thanks, dear.
- Where are the Guimaras mangoes?

464
00:33:12,968 --> 00:33:16,645
Florence, we have a problem.

465
00:33:18,447 --> 00:33:21,902
We have a problem with the mangoes.

466
00:33:21,902 --> 00:33:23,343
Why?

467
00:33:23,343 --> 00:33:26,230
Don't tell me those are not Guimaras Mangoes.

468
00:33:26,230 --> 00:33:29,199
Tristan only wants Guimaras Mangoes,

469
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:32,366
the sweetest mangoes in the whole world.

470
00:33:32,367 --> 00:33:34,347
The universe, rather.

471
00:33:34,347 --> 00:33:37,891
Of course, let me finish first.

472
00:33:37,891 --> 00:33:40,144
These are Guimaras Mangoes,

473
00:33:40,144 --> 00:33:44,958
but our problem is
we might just do two mango pies.

474
00:33:44,958 --> 00:33:50,253
Because on our way back here,
Iking ate the mangoes.

475
00:33:50,253 --> 00:33:51,941
Originally, we had two baskets.

476
00:33:51,941 --> 00:33:53,745
Now we only have one.

477
00:33:54,706 --> 00:33:59,212
I can't stop myself. It's delicious.

478
00:33:59,212 --> 00:34:01,399
As a matter of fact,

479
00:34:01,400 --> 00:34:03,132
there's a rumor...

480
00:34:03,133 --> 00:34:06,300
that Guimaras Mangoes are served

481
00:34:06,300 --> 00:34:10,016
in the Buckingham Palace of Queen Elizabeth.

482
00:34:10,016 --> 00:34:13,086
If the Queen ate the mangoes,
what more than I,

483
00:34:13,086 --> 00:34:16,233
who's just a commoner?

484
00:34:18,158 --> 00:34:19,588
Okay, that's enough,

485
00:34:19,588 --> 00:34:22,943
but you're no longer allowed
to eat mango pie.

486
00:34:24,431 --> 00:34:27,067
- There you go.
- Fair enough.

487
00:34:27,067 --> 00:34:28,542
By the way Florence,

488
00:34:28,542 --> 00:34:32,574
you have to make sure
that your pie is crusty and not crunchy.

489
00:34:32,574 --> 00:34:35,542
That's how Tristan wants it, okay?

490
00:34:35,542 --> 00:34:37,010
Wait.

491
00:34:37,010 --> 00:34:39,179
What's the difference?

492
00:34:39,179 --> 00:34:41,998
That's just the same, right?

493
00:34:42,956 --> 00:34:47,370
Because the sound is crunchy
when what you're eating is crusty.

494
00:34:49,256 --> 00:34:54,794
But it seems it's not okay
if it's not crunchy and crusty?

495
00:34:54,794 --> 00:34:57,336
Mother, I'll take care of that

496
00:34:57,336 --> 00:35:01,449
because I know the secret
to making it crusty but not crunchy.

497
00:35:19,719 --> 00:35:21,704
There's your mango pie.

498
00:35:21,704 --> 00:35:23,267
I've perfected that already.

499
00:35:23,267 --> 00:35:24,524
Enjoy it over there.

500
00:35:24,524 --> 00:35:27,661
Tristan, now that you're there,
you have no excuse.

501
00:35:27,661 --> 00:35:29,296
Be with your grandmother.

502
00:35:29,296 --> 00:35:31,364
Remember, we're the Ferells.

503
00:35:31,364 --> 00:35:33,333
How about you, guys?

504
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:35,952
Don't you have something to say to that guy?

505
00:35:36,670 --> 00:35:38,571
Bro, don't worry.

506
00:35:38,571 --> 00:35:40,640
I made sure to delete your browsing history

507
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:44,578
so no one would know
what videos you are watching.

508
00:35:47,387 --> 00:35:49,649
Bro, you're a fool.

509
00:35:49,649 --> 00:35:53,320
I owe GU a huge amount of money,
and they're asking me to pay...

510
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:55,571
because you ate a lot of brownies.

511
00:35:57,656 --> 00:36:01,061
Don't worry, Bro. Camille is perfectly fine.

512
00:36:01,061 --> 00:36:03,029
Aira, Lina, and Antonia are always with her.

513
00:36:03,029 --> 00:36:05,966
And I'm making sure
she has someone to talk to.

514
00:36:05,966 --> 00:36:08,417
Don't worry. We'll take care of it.

515
00:36:09,736 --> 00:36:11,307
Say hi to dad.

516
00:36:11,972 --> 00:36:13,740
I'm sorry.

517
00:36:13,740 --> 00:36:16,443
Just be patient with his jokes.

518
00:36:16,443 --> 00:36:19,061
And please tell him that we're okay here...

519
00:36:19,855 --> 00:36:21,774
and that there's no need to worry.

520
00:36:22,749 --> 00:36:25,375
No one needs to knock on my heart.

521
00:36:29,456 --> 00:36:31,680
It's now open to love.

522
00:36:34,194 --> 00:36:36,329
Tristan, my child.

523
00:36:36,329 --> 00:36:39,415
Thank you so much for all the memories.

524
00:36:40,567 --> 00:36:41,951
Tristan...

525
00:36:42,705 --> 00:36:45,081
I'll take care of your car.

526
00:36:46,639 --> 00:36:52,808
Tristan, I'm sorry
I ate your Guimaras Mangoes.

527
00:36:53,513 --> 00:36:55,849
I will miss your muscles.

528
00:36:55,849 --> 00:36:57,299
Tristan...

529
00:36:58,618 --> 00:37:01,368
I will miss your mango pies.

530
00:37:03,923 --> 00:37:06,026
Sir Tristan...

531
00:37:06,026 --> 00:37:09,129
we'll always remember you.

532
00:37:09,129 --> 00:37:13,556
With my first bite of mango pie,
that's for you.

533
00:37:14,834 --> 00:37:16,569
Tristan...

534
00:37:16,569 --> 00:37:21,123
I'll consider it a huge debt of gratitude
for saving my daughter.

535
00:37:22,442 --> 00:37:25,394
Thank you so much, Tristan.

536
00:37:26,146 --> 00:37:29,434
I will now take care of your family.

537
00:37:36,456 --> 00:37:38,925
You're open to love?

538
00:37:38,925 --> 00:37:41,577
Shouldn't be that closed already?

539
00:37:42,481 --> 00:37:44,499
Am I not enough?

540
00:37:45,328 --> 00:37:47,333
It's enough...

541
00:37:47,333 --> 00:37:49,235
but you're leaving.

542
00:37:49,235 --> 00:37:54,828
That's why I'm keeping it open,
waiting for your return.

543
00:37:58,411 --> 00:38:03,432
I'm sorry, Nero,
but I really need to do this.

544
00:38:04,117 --> 00:38:11,458
Actually, Daddy said
I can stay and continue with Gyronella.

545
00:38:11,458 --> 00:38:13,827
But I thought,

546
00:38:13,827 --> 00:38:19,548
maybe this is the perfect time and opportunity
to go abroad first.

547
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:26,539
He also promised that he'll stop working,
so he can have time for me.

548
00:38:26,539 --> 00:38:30,796
So, we have more time to bond.

549
00:38:31,411 --> 00:38:33,652
I can get to know him better,

550
00:38:33,652 --> 00:38:38,267
and I'll ask him to tell me
about his love story with Mommy.

551
00:38:41,116 --> 00:38:43,134
What about Mother and Father?

552
00:38:44,924 --> 00:38:48,978
I want to bring them, but...

553
00:38:49,635 --> 00:38:53,121
it's their decision not to go.

554
00:38:53,833 --> 00:38:56,528
I've been with them for 18 years,

555
00:38:56,528 --> 00:39:01,857
that's why it's not bad
if I'm with Daddy in the meantime next year.

556
00:39:05,078 --> 00:39:07,136
I'm sorry, Nero.

557
00:39:08,084 --> 00:39:10,369
This is my decision.

558
00:39:11,251 --> 00:39:14,181
I need to complete my story.

559
00:39:17,941 --> 00:39:20,838
It doesn't matter how long it takes.

560
00:39:22,462 --> 00:39:24,947
I will wait for you, Florence.

561
00:39:26,077 --> 00:39:29,642
I will wait for you, until the end of time.

562
00:39:30,465 --> 00:39:34,283
Wow. You're an English poet now.

563
00:39:37,450 --> 00:39:42,699
But once I'm ready, I'll come back.

564
00:39:42,699 --> 00:39:45,552
And if you will really wait for me,

565
00:39:45,552 --> 00:39:48,437
you'll have my heart completely.

566
00:39:50,256 --> 00:39:52,072
It should be.

567
00:39:53,692 --> 00:39:55,628
A white guy might flirt with you.

568
00:39:55,628 --> 00:39:57,330
If so, I will beat him.

569
00:39:57,330 --> 00:39:58,531
Wow.

570
00:39:58,531 --> 00:39:59,766
Violent.

571
00:39:59,766 --> 00:40:01,513
I'm just telling you.

572
00:40:02,427 --> 00:40:04,737
Who knows?

573
00:40:04,737 --> 00:40:10,125
When I come back,
I will not only give you my heart...

574
00:40:11,309 --> 00:40:12,897
What else?

575
00:40:14,013 --> 00:40:18,959
Who knows? I'm ready to give you my...

576
00:40:22,255 --> 00:40:24,403
Next time...

577
00:40:25,725 --> 00:40:27,731
you won't have a choice.

578
00:40:36,803 --> 00:40:38,104
Our lips might touch.

579
00:40:38,104 --> 00:40:39,872
I'm not yet ready.

580
00:40:39,872 --> 00:40:41,908
- Next time?
- Next time.

581
00:40:41,908 --> 00:40:43,843
Next time, when I come back.

582
00:40:43,843 --> 00:40:45,278
You will no longer have a choice.

583
00:40:45,278 --> 00:40:46,813
I will delay my return.

584
00:40:46,813 --> 00:40:48,796
No, please don't.

585
00:41:25,285 --> 00:41:28,919
<i>They said it's hard to say goodbye.</i>

586
00:41:38,831 --> 00:41:44,075
What they didn't know is
that waiting is more difficult than goodbye.

587
00:42:27,113 --> 00:42:30,043
<i>They said it's hard to say goodbye.</i>

588
00:42:30,775 --> 00:42:35,392
<i>What they didn't know is
that waiting is more difficult than goodbye.</i>

589
00:42:36,456 --> 00:42:39,592
- Hi!
- Hello.

590
00:42:39,592 --> 00:42:42,195
- I miss you, guys.
- Hello. Hey.

591
00:42:42,195 --> 00:42:46,010
- Hey, handsome man!
- Hey!

592
00:42:46,010 --> 00:42:47,744
Hi!

593
00:42:53,462 --> 00:42:57,744
<i>You need to smile and pretend</i>

594
00:42:57,744 --> 00:43:00,416
<i>that every day that passes by...</i>

595
00:43:01,215 --> 00:43:03,833
<i>it's okay not to see you.</i>

596
00:43:04,450 --> 00:43:08,322
<i>That I can face everything without you.</i>

597
00:43:13,159 --> 00:43:14,694
<i>But it's hard, Florence.</i>

598
00:43:14,694 --> 00:43:17,416
<i>It's difficult
because of the memories you left.</i>

599
00:43:18,297 --> 00:43:20,867
<i>The stories...</i>

600
00:43:20,867 --> 00:43:23,517
<i>laughter...</i>

601
00:43:23,517 --> 00:43:26,239
<i>goofing around moments...</i>

602
00:43:26,239 --> 00:43:31,061
<i>and all the scenes remind me
of how we were once happy.</i>

603
00:43:31,835 --> 00:43:34,496
<i>And convinced us that it's possible...</i>

604
00:43:35,481 --> 00:43:39,046
<i>to make the world more colorful
every time I'm with you.</i>

605
00:43:40,288 --> 00:43:42,462
<i>The ironic thing, Florence,</i>

606
00:43:42,462 --> 00:43:46,990
<i>is that these memories
that make my longing deeper...</i>

607
00:43:46,990 --> 00:43:49,966
<i>are the same memories that comfort me.</i>

608
00:43:50,927 --> 00:43:52,945
<i>And it makes me believe.</i>

609
00:43:53,664 --> 00:43:55,766
<i>It gives me hope...</i>

610
00:43:55,767 --> 00:43:59,533
<i>that this chapter is
not the end of our story.</i>

611
00:44:00,447 --> 00:44:04,986
<i>As we turn another page in our story,</i>

612
00:44:06,412 --> 00:44:10,869
<i>what's waiting for me is a world
where our hands are holding each other.</i>

613
00:44:12,553 --> 00:44:16,507
<i>We're together,
helping each other complete our story.</i>

614
00:44:20,326 --> 00:44:22,666
<i>I cannot wait, Florence...</i>

615
00:44:22,667 --> 00:44:25,606
<i>I can't wait to see you again.</i>

616
00:44:26,862 --> 00:44:28,981
<i>To hug you.</i>

617
00:44:28,981 --> 00:44:32,604
<i>I cannot wait
to spend the rest of my life with you.</i>

618
00:44:33,818 --> 00:44:35,636
<i>I will wait...</i>

619
00:44:36,668 --> 00:44:38,990
<i>for your return.</i>

620
00:44:40,446 --> 00:44:43,015
<i>But it's hard, Florence.</i>

621
00:44:43,015 --> 00:44:45,374
<i>It's so difficult without you.</i>

622
00:44:46,717 --> 00:44:48,854
<i>But don't worry.</i>

623
00:44:48,855 --> 00:44:51,421
<i>I'm always looking for a way...</i>

624
00:44:52,319 --> 00:44:56,546
<i>to relieve the sadness and longing.</i>

625
00:44:57,865 --> 00:45:02,463
<i>But the truth is,
you can't relieve the longing.</i>

626
00:45:03,262 --> 00:45:06,448
<i>We're just convincing ourselves...</i>

627
00:45:07,347 --> 00:45:10,343
<i>that tomorrow or the day after...</i>

628
00:45:10,343 --> 00:45:13,853
<i>all the heaviness in our hearts will go away.</i>

629
00:45:15,845 --> 00:45:20,009
<i>I pray that one morning I'll wake up...</i>

630
00:45:21,120 --> 00:45:24,039
<i>and that my beloved has returned.</i>

631
00:45:25,893 --> 00:45:29,746
<i>And we can start again with a new chance...</i>

632
00:45:30,836 --> 00:45:32,769
<i>to love.</i>

633
00:46:17,276 --> 00:46:21,147
<i>Hello, Nero! I'm back!</i>

634
00:46:21,147 --> 00:46:22,981
Florence?

635
00:47:13,799 --> 00:47:15,501
I'm just happy that you're here.

636
00:47:15,501 --> 00:47:18,148
So, let's see each other tomorrow?

637
00:47:21,407 --> 00:47:22,661
Go ahead and end the call.

638
00:47:22,661 --> 00:47:23,943
<i>You end it first.</i>

639
00:47:23,943 --> 00:47:25,544
Hey, the last time, it was me.

640
00:47:25,544 --> 00:47:26,912
<i>Then you do it again.</i>

641
00:47:26,912 --> 00:47:28,347
You're unfair.

642
00:47:28,347 --> 00:47:29,856
<i>Hurry.</i>

643
00:47:32,885 --> 00:47:34,994
- Go ahead and end the call.
- <i>You go first.</i>

644
00:47:34,994 --> 00:47:36,358
Don't be a cheater, Florence.

645
00:47:36,358 --> 00:47:38,758
<i>Okay, here it goes. Bye.</i>

646
00:47:38,758 --> 00:47:40,108
Bye-bye.

647
00:47:53,806 --> 00:47:55,467
Tristan?
